<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">Hello All,<o:p></o:p><=
/span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">There is an informal r=
ule of thumb that one step of DR is acceptable at a fusion joint.<o:p></o:p=
></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">There is no official d=
ocumentation of this as a recommended practice in any industry standard or =
at the PPI however.&nbsp; It is all word of mouth.&nbsp; The understanding =
is that it would be at the user=92s risk.&nbsp;
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">The general availabili=
ty of fittings with machined ends (where the ends are machined to match the=
 pipe) is for the purpose of matching at the joint with the pipe.&nbsp; Thi=
s can be done with fabricated and molded
 fittings.&nbsp; We have the capability to do this and have done it.&nbsp; =
Pricing for fabricated fittings are in the price sheets.&nbsp; Fittings wit=
h machined ends will cost more.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">The fusion parameters =
would have to be adjusted &nbsp;for mismatching DR=92s but there is no offi=
cial industry guideline for this either.&nbsp; Again this is at user=92s ri=
sk.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">When the mismatch gets=
 too great there are two problems that occur.&nbsp; The fusion joint qualit=
y is questionable and the creation of a geometric stress riser (the step it=
self).&nbsp; This is mostly an issue at fitting
 to pipe connections.&nbsp; The fusion joint quality is questionable becaus=
e the ideal fusion parameters are more different for the larger mismatch.<o=
:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">Brandon Wheeler of Nup=
i has long experience with these matters working at JM Eagles fitting plant=
.&nbsp; He says he has seen ample evidence from failures that two DR steps =
is too much.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">Defining a DR step has=
 some peculiarities because there are =93half step=94 DR=92s<o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">From thicker to thinne=
r the full step DR=92s for IPS pipe go like this:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">7<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">9<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">11<o:p></o:p></span></=
p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">13.5<o:p></o:p></span>=
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">17<o:p></o:p></span></=
p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">21<o:p></o:p></span></=
p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">26<o:p></o:p></span></=
p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">32.5<o:p></o:p></span>=
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">DR 15.5 is a =93half s=
tep=94 DR.&nbsp; The rule of thumb would say a DR11 fitting should have end=
s machined to DR 15.5 or at least to DR 13.5 when used with DR 15.5 pipe.<o=
:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">Our thoughts on this i=
f asked:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-left:.5in"><span style=3D"color:#1F4=
97D">Harco advises that good practice is to match the ends at a joint.&nbsp=
; There is an unofficial rule of thumb that a mismatch of one DR step can b=
e acceptable but to do so would be the users
 decision and risk.&nbsp; Our observation to date in the golf application i=
s that one step in DR across a joint seems not to have resulted in problems=
 to this date.&nbsp; We must caution that the experience of PE systems in g=
olf applications is very short and that the
 problems may not manifest themselves for some time. &nbsp;It is only in th=
e last 4 years that pipe thinner than DR 11 has been in regular use.&nbsp; =
These systems would use DR13.5 pipe and DR11 fittings.<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:#1F497D">John<o:p></o:p></span>=
</p>
